Refused: ACP's key-order rule on ElicitationSchema.properties, with ElicitationSchema a
union whose own properties only its variants' structs hold. resolveKeyOrders already
refused it before 0049's G20 fix, and this case guards that
(0049-PLAN-generator-fixes.md, phase 6, deviation 1).

-- meta.json --
{"version": 1, "agentMethods": {}, "clientMethods": {}, "protocolMethods": {"cancel_request": "$/cancel_request"}}
-- schema.json --
{"$defs": {
  "ElicitationSchema": {"properties": {"properties": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {"type": "string"}}},
    "anyOf": [{"title": "A", "type": "object", "properties": {"a": {"type": "string"}}}, {"title": "B", "type": "object", "properties": {"b": {"type": "string"}}}]},
  "CancelRequestNotification": {"type": "object", "x-side": "protocol", "x-method": "$/cancel_request"}
}}
-- want.err --
ElicitationSchema.properties: a key-order rule needs a property of an object
